{
  "item": [
    {
      "id": "6877ffc9-8960-4ef3-8ef6-4bdc6607ac73",
      "name": "Environment Backups",
      "description": {
        "content": "A snapshot is a complete backup of an environment, including all the\npersistent data from all services running in an environment and all\nfiles present in mounted volumes.\n\nThese endpoints can be used to trigger the creation of new backups,\nget information about existing backups, delete existing backups or\nrestore a backup.\nMore information about backups can be found in our\n[documentation](https://docs.upsun.com/anchors/environments/backup/).\n",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
